      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — extracting the long opaque strings as named constants, removing unused imports/fields, reusing the static `UNLIMITED_DISTANCE` constant, and splitting the assertions into clearly-named variables.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the two long opaque strings as named constants (`LEFT_INPUT`/`RIGHT_INPUT`), introduces an `EXPECTED_DISTANCE` constant for the magic number `20`, reuses the existing `UNLIMITED_DISTANCE` static field instead of a redundant local variable, separates the two assertions into clearly-named result variables, and removes all unused imports."
